<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Toki Yorinari</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1502">1502</a>–<a href="/years/1582">1582</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Toki Yorinari was the last of the Toki family to hold the office of military governor (shugo) of Mino province in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>. Raised to power with the help of his retainer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saito-dosan">Saito Dosan</a>, he was driven out by Dosan around 1542, and after a brief return with outside help he was finally expelled in 1552. He spent his last decades in exile.</p></div>
